### BGP Configuration

```junos
set protocols bgp group my-bgp {
    local-as none;
}

set protocols bgp group my-bgp neighbor 192.168.1.1 remote-as 65000;
```

### OSPF Configuration

```junos
set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 router-id 192.168.1.1;

set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface ge-0/0/0.0;
set protocols ospf area 0.0.0.0 interface ge-0/0/1.0;

set protocols ospf area 64 router-id 192.168.1.1;

set protocols ospf area 64 interface ge-0/0/0.0;
set protocols ospf area 64 interface ge-0/0/1.0;
```

### VLAN Creation and Access Ports Assignment

Assuming you have two VLANs: `VLAN1` and `VLAN2`, and you want to assign access ports to them on your Juniper device.

#### VLAN 1

```junos
set interfaces ge-0/0/0 unit 0 vlan-id 1;
set interfaces ge-0/0/1 unit 0 vlan-id 1;
```

#### VLAN 2

```junos
set interfaces ge-0/0/0 unit 1 vlan-id 2;
set interfaces ge-0/0/1 unit 1 vlan-id 2;
```

### Full Configuration Example

Here's a complete example that includes all the above configurations:

```junos
set system hostname my-juniper-router

set chassis family ethernet-switching

set interfaces ge-0/0/0 unit 0 description "Access Port 1"
set interfaces ge-0/0/0 unit 0 vlan-id 1

set interfaces ge-0/0/1 unit 0 description "Access Port 2"
set interfaces ge-0/0/1 unit 0 vlan-id 1

